**suggestion:** Assumes 3-component coord; consider guarding against unexpected coord shapes

This assumes `orig` is always a vec3 and blindly reads channels 0–2, which matches the current cube-to-2d lowering. If coord arity changes in the future (extra W, different dimensionality), this could lead to invalid accesses. Please add a defensive guard (e.g., `assert(orig->num_components >= 3)` or normalize with `nir_trim_vector`/`nir_swizzle`) to make this more resilient to NIR layout changes.

Suggested implementation:

```c
            nir_builder b = nir_builder_at(nir_before_instr(instr));
            nir_def *orig = tex->src[coord_index].src.ssa;
            assert(orig->num_components >= 3);
            nir_def *normalized = nir_vec3(&b,
               nir_fadd_imm(&b, nir_channel(&b, orig, 0), -1.0f),
               nir_fadd_imm(&b, nir_channel(&b, orig, 1), -1.0f),
               nir_channel(&b, orig, 2));
            nir_src_rewrite(&tex->src[coord_index].src, normalized);
            impl_progress = true;

```

Ensure `#include <assert.h>` is present at the top of `src/amd/terascale/vulkan/terakan_shader.c` (or that a project-local assert header is already included) so that `assert` is available.

